          "filename": "Hugh llewelyn 3420 (5963627632).jpg",
          "caption": "Southern Pacific (ex-El Paso &amp; South Western RR - which had 64 of this design) Class \"C-19\" 2-8-0 No.3420 built by Baldwin in 1904 with Vanderbilt tender at El Paso, 8/70. 387 of the various \"C\" Classes were built: 319 for SP (and it's many minor subsidiaries such as the EP &amp; SW) (1901-19) and 68 for it's main subsidiary T&amp;NO (1904-22) by the railroads own shops and ALCO, Baldwin &amp; Lima. The design was their standard freight loco for many years. It was a E Roland Harriman \"Common Standard\" design for his many railroads.",
          "alt": "Southern Pacific (ex-El Paso &amp; South Western RR - which had 64 of this design) Class \"C-19\" 2-8-0 No.3420 built by Baldwin in 1904 with Vanderbilt tender at El Paso, 8/70. 387 of the various \"C\" Classes were built: 319 for SP (and it's many minor subsidiaries such as the EP &amp; SW) (1901-19) and 68 for it's main subsidiary T&amp;NO (1904-22) by the railroads own shops and ALCO, Baldwin &amp; Lima. The design was their standard freight loco for many years. It was a E Roland Harriman \"Common Standard\" design for his many railroads.",
          "width": 2520,
